<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Wtimewarp (255)</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>wtimewarp &lt;seconds&gt;
</pre>
<p>Example:
</p>
<pre>wtimewarp 600
</pre>
<p>Runs the game as fast as the server can for that many seconds of game 
time: the pause between heartbeats is dropped, so ten minutes of the 
game's life (resets, regeneration, weather, DIL programs waiting) may pass 
in a few real seconds. Then the game goes back to its normal speed, and 
"Ending time warp, back to normal game speed." is written to the log.
</p><p>Meant for testing, for example to see what a zone does over hours. 
Everyone in the game lives through the warp too. While it lasts, 
<a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Wstat</a> world shows the game as time-warped. It is logged.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Wstat</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Reset</a>
</pre>




</div>